+# B1930 — The foundation at version 1.68: its paths into the moved historical folders
+
+*2026-11-13. Paths only; no computation is made here and no measured number is read. The record's historical folders
+moved under `docs/archive/` in the same patch (`docs/REORGANIZATIONS.md`, its third entry; card C18 of the building
+session, approved by main in its message M28 to that session, which asked that the foundation's paths change by a
+version written by the foundation's own script). This page, the script and the lock were put together by the building
+session; main lands the arc after its own check. 0 of 19.*
+
+## 1. The answer first
+
+- **Six paths of the foundation's living sections (§§ 0 to 8) point into the moved folders: four into `philosophy/`,
+  one into `paths/`, one into `speculations/`. Each now names its file under `docs/archive/`.** Main's message counted
+  three into `philosophy/`; a search of the page found four, and the other two folders' one each.
+- The version log (§ 10) is dated text: it keeps its paths as written, and the path check resolves them through the
+  log of moves, which names the commit that last held every moved file at its old place.
+- No item is added. No status changes. No word but the paths changes; the version's line reads 1.68, and its entry
+  stands above that of 1.67.
+
+## Seen first
+
+Not a result about the object: a change of paths. The sweep of the foundation for paths into the moved folders is the
+script's own check: each of the six stands once in §§ 0 to 8 and none is left there; the version log's paths are left as
+written. The record's other pages that cite the moved folders are the move's (its script's list of living pages, and the
+measurement of card C18, `relays/advisor_2026-11-10_audit/c18/MEASUREMENT.md`).
+
+**Literature:** none bears on it; it changes paths and states nothing about the object.
+
+## 2. How it was made
+
+`verification/write_version_1_68.py` holds no sentence of the foundation. It names the six paths, checks that each
+stands once in §§ 0 to 8, puts `docs/archive/` before each, checks that none is left, adds the entry of the log above
+1.67's and moves the version's line. Run without `--write` it writes nothing.
+
+## 3. The lock
+
+`verification/test_b1930_the_foundation_at_version_1_68.py`: the page is at 1.68; each of the six paths names a file
+that exists under `docs/archive/`, and none stands at its old place in §§ 0 to 8; the entry is above 1.67's; and the
+script, applied to the page with this version taken back, gives the page as it stands. Planted: a path left at its old
+place; a seventh path into a moved folder added to § 1. Each is refused.
+
+## 4. What this is not
+
+It does not read the moved folders, judge them or change them. Whether a philosophy passage is motivation or premise
+is said where it was said: the foundation's § 1 and each passage's header.
